---

<section class="py-20 px-6 bg-surface/50" aria-labelledby="method-heading">
	<div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
		<header class="text-center mb-16">
			<h2 id="method-heading" class="text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-bold text-text-heading mb-6">
				The Method
			</h2>
			<p class="text-xl text-text-body max-w-3xl mx-auto">
				How I diagnose broken operations and rebuild them to last.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
			<!-- Method Overview -->
			<div class="space-y-6">
				<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-heading">
					How I Think About Operations
				</h3>
				<p class="text-text-body leading-relaxed">
					When operations break, it's rarely the process—it's the information flow. 
					Payroll errors, compliance gaps, inventory messes—these are symptoms of 
					broken information systems. I don't just patch the process; I rebuild 
					the foundation so things work right going forward.
				</p>
				<p class="text-text-body leading-relaxed">
					I dig into where information actually flows (or doesn't), find the breaks, 
					and build systems that make knowledge visible and usable across the team. 
					Same approach worked at Sonic, Grandlux, and KLW—because the problem 
					is always the same: broken information flow.
				</p>
				<p class="text-text-heading font-medium italic border-l-4 border-teal pl-4 my-4">
					My core skill: building systems that make organizational knowledge visible 
					and actionable—so teams stop scrambling and start executing.
				</p>
				<a 
					href="/methodology" 
					class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-teal-text hover:text-teal-text/90 font-medium transition-colors duration-200 min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px] focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-teal-text focus:ring-offset-2 focus:ring-offset-bg rounded"
				>
					Explore the Methodology
					<svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
						<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"></path>
					</svg>
				</a>
			</div>

			<!-- Method Pillars -->
			<div class="space-y-6">
				<div class="bg-bg border border-border rounded-lg p-6">
					<h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-heading mb-3">Dig Into the Problem</h4>
					<p class="text-text-body text-sm leading-relaxed">
						I investigate what's actually breaking and why. Look at the data, 
						trace the information flow, find the root cause before proposing fixes.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="bg-bg border border-border rounded-lg p-6">
					<h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-heading mb-3">Rebuild the System</h4>
					<p class="text-text-body text-sm leading-relaxed">
						Design information systems with proper controls and automation that 
						prevent errors instead of just catching them after the fact.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="bg-bg border border-border rounded-lg p-6">
					<h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-heading mb-3">Make It Work in Practice</h4>
					<p class="text-text-body text-sm leading-relaxed">
						New systems have to work with real operations and real people. I ensure 
						smooth rollout, business continuity, and actual team adoption—not just 
						theoretical perfection.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
